            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Every source can have \"current working directory\". So with `builtin.files()` you can do `MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = { cwd = '../foo/bar' } })`.\r\n\r\nIf you plan to do that often interactively, you can [modify `files` in registry](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a118a964c94543c06d8b1f2f7542535dd2e19d36/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1186-L1191) and use `:Pick files cwd='../foo/bar'`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Every source can have \"current working directory\". So with <code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.files()</code> you can do <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = { cwd = '../foo/bar' } })</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you plan to do that often interactively, you can <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a118a964c94543c06d8b1f2f7542535dd2e19d36/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1186-L1191\">modify <code class=\"notranslate\">files</code> in registry</a> and use <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick files cwd='../foo/bar'</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Every source can have \"current working directory\". So with builtin.files() you can do MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = { cwd = '../foo/bar' } }).\nIf you plan to do that often interactively, you can modify files in registry and use :Pick files cwd='../foo/bar'.",
